{"id":"evil-merodach","name":"Evil-Merodach","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:evil-merodach"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Evil-merodach","text":"Merodach’s man, the son and successor of Nebuchadnezzar, king of Babylon (2 Kings 25:27; Jer. 52:31, 34). He seems to have reigned but two years (B.C. 562-560). Influenced probably by Daniel, he showed kindness to Jehoiachin, who had been a prisoner in Babylon for thirty-seven years. He released him, and “spoke kindly to him.” He was murdered by Nergal-sharezer=Neriglissar, his brother-in-law, who succeeded him (Jer. 39:3, 13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8548","lemma":"תָּמִיד","xlit":"tâmîyd","gloss":"continuance","kjv":"alway, continual, daily, ever","count":4,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H2416","lemma":"חַי","xlit":"chay","gloss":"alive","kjv":"age, alive, appetite, beast","count":4,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":6,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H3117","lemma":"יוֹם","xlit":"yôwm","gloss":"a day , whether literal , or figurative","kjv":"age, always, chronicals, continually","count":4,"share":0.5}],"verses":["2Kgs.25.29","2Kgs.25.30","Jer.52.33","Jer.52.34","2Kgs.25.27","2Kgs.25.28","Jer.52.31","Jer.52.32"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"jehoiachin","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.195,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"captive","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.043,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"kindness","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.02,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"animals","type":"lexical","strong":"H2416","why":"both lead with חַי (H2416)"},{"id":"beard","type":"lexical","strong":"H2416","why":"both lead with חַי (H2416)"},{"id":"life-natural","type":"lexical","strong":"H2416","why":"both lead with חַ